  "name": "Mudiyettu (Kerala Kali ritual-drama music)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Mudiyettu is a ritual dance-drama of central Kerala enacting the battle of the goddess Kali with the demon Darika, performed by the Marar and Kuruppu communities in the Bhagavati temples (kavu) of villages along the Chalakudy, Periyar and Moovattupuzha rivers after the summer harvest. It begins with a drawing of Kali (kalam) in coloured powders and is carried by chenda drumming, ilathalam cymbals and songs. It is inscribed on UNESCO's Representative List of the Intangible Cultural Heritage.",
